---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import MulchCalculator from '../components/MulchCalculator';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { getLangFromUrl, useTranslations } from '../i18n/utils';
import { Layers, Maximize2, DollarSign } from 'lucide-react';

const lang = getLangFromUrl(Astro.url);
const t = useTranslations(lang);
---

<Layout>
	<Nav lang={lang} />

	<main>
		<section id="calculator" class="relative overflow-hidden bg-canvas px-4 sm:px-6 py-14 sm:py-20 border-b border-hairline">
			<div class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-[420px] mesh-gradient opacity-35 pointer-events-none"></div>
			<div class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-hairline-strong to-transparent"></div>
			<div class="relative max-w-6xl mx-auto space-y-12">
				<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center space-y-6">
					<div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-hairline-strong bg-canvas/80 px-4 py-2 shadow-sm backdrop-blur">
						<span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-cyan-deep"></span>
						<p class="caption-mono text-mute">MULCH CALCULATOR</p>
					</div>
					<h1 class="display-xl text-ink max-w-3xl mx-auto">{t('calc.title')} Calculate mulch yards, bags, and cost in one fast tool.</h1>
					<p class="body-lg text-body max-w-2xl mx-auto">
						{t('calc.subtitle')} A clean, mobile-first mulch calculator for garden beds, tree rings, playground areas, and landscape coverage. Enter your shape, depth, material type, and bag size to estimate cubic yards, bags, and cost instantly.
					</p>
					<div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3 pt-2">
						<span class="caption-mono rounded-full border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft px-3 py-1 text-mute">Cubic yards</span>
						<span class="caption-mono rounded-full border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft px-3 py-1 text-mute">Bags</span>
						<span class="caption-mono rounded-full border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft px-3 py-1 text-mute">Cost estimate</span>
						<span class="caption-mono rounded-full border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft px-3 py-1 text-mute">Garden beds</span>
					</div>
				</div>

				<MulchCalculator client:load lang={lang} />
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="bg-canvas-soft px-4 sm:px-6 py-16 sm:py-20 border-b border-hairline">
			<div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 lg:gap-6">
				<article class="classical-card rounded-lg p-6 sm:p-7 space-y-4">
					<div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-sm bg-cyan-soft border border-cyan-deep/20 flex items-center justify-center">
						<Layers className="w-5 h-5 text-cyan-deep" />
					</div>
					<h2 class="display-sm text-ink">Multi-area support</h2>
					<p class="body-sm text-body">Calculate multiple distinct garden beds simultaneously and get a combined total for your entire project.</p>
				</article>

				<article class="classical-card rounded-lg p-6 sm:p-7 space-y-4">
					<div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-sm bg-violet-soft border border-violet-deep/20 flex items-center justify-center">
						<Maximize2 className="w-5 h-5 text-violet-deep" />
					</div>
					<h2 class="display-sm text-ink">Precision shapes</h2>
					<p class="body-sm text-body">Calculate volume for rectangles, circles, and triangles with geometric accuracy for any landscape design.</p>
				</article>

				<article class="classical-card rounded-lg p-6 sm:p-7 space-y-4">
					<div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-sm bg-warning-soft border border-warning-deep/20 flex items-center justify-center">
						<DollarSign className="w-5 h-5 text-warning-deep" />
					</div>
					<h2 class="display-sm text-ink">Cost analysis</h2>
					<p class="body-sm text-body">Instantly compare costs between bulk deliveries and standard bag sizes for smarter budgeting.</p>
				</article>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="bg-canvas border-b border-hairline px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6">
				<p class="body-md text-body">Need to estimate gravel for a driveway or path?</p>
				<a href={lang === 'en' ? '/gravel-calculator' : `/${lang}/gravel-calculator`} class="inline-flex items-center justify-center classical-button h-10 px-5 shrink-0">
					Try the Gravel Calculator
				</a>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="bg-canvas px-6 py-20">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-neutral max-w-none
				prose-headings:font-geist prose-headings:font-semibold prose-headings:tracking-tighter
				prose-h2:text-display-md prose-h2:text-ink
				prose-h3:text-display-sm prose-h3:text-ink
				prose-p:text-body-md prose-p:text-body prose-p:leading-relaxed
				prose-li:text-body-sm prose-li:text-body
				prose-strong:text-ink">
				<h2>Landscape Material Calculators Built for Real Projects</h2>
				<p>
					Mulchcalculator1.com is designed to help homeowners, landscapers, and contractors estimate outdoor materials with confidence before they buy. The main <strong>mulch calculator</strong> focuses on garden beds, tree rings, playground areas, and decorative landscape coverage, while our <a href={lang === 'en' ? '/gravel-calculator' : `/${lang}/gravel-calculator`}>gravel calculator</a> helps plan driveways, paths, patios, paver bases, and stone projects. Both tools are built around practical job-site math: measure the area, choose a depth, compare bulk and bagged material, and order with less waste.
				</p>
				<p>
					A good calculator should do more than display one number. Real landscape projects often require several buying formats. Mulch is commonly sold by cubic yard or bag, while gravel can be sold by cubic yard, ton, or bag depending on the supplier. That is why our tools include high-value outputs for cubic yards, cubic feet, cubic meters, and bag count. If you are searching for a <strong>mulch calculator yards</strong> tool, a <strong>mulch calculator bags</strong> estimator, or a <strong>mulch calculator lowes</strong> companion, this page gives you a faster way to compare all of those ordering units in one place.
				</p>
				<h3>Why accurate material estimates matter</h3>
				<p>
					Buying too little material can delay a project, create color mismatch between separate deliveries, and add extra delivery fees. Buying too much can leave piles of unused mulch, pea gravel, or crushed stone that are difficult to store or remove. Accurate estimates also help with budgeting because they let you compare bulk delivery against retail bags before you commit. For small garden beds, bags may be convenient. For a long driveway, bulk gravel is usually more efficient. The calculator workflow makes those tradeoffs clear on desktop and mobile devices.
				</p>
				<p>
					Depth is especially important. A thin mulch layer may not suppress weeds or retain moisture effectively, while an overly deep layer can harm plants. Gravel projects have the same issue: a decorative path may only need a shallow layer, but a driveway usually needs more depth and stronger base material. The <strong>mulch calculator</strong> accounts for depth, density, and bag size so your estimate better reflects real installation conditions. It can also be used as a <strong>bark mulch calculator</strong> for organic materials or a <strong>playground mulch calculator</strong> for deeper safety surfacing.
				</p>
				<h3>Built for speed, clarity, and mobile use</h3>
				<p>
					Many calculator websites are cluttered with slow layouts, confusing forms, and hard-to-read results. This website is intentionally cleaner. The calculators load quickly, keep the most important inputs near the top, and display results in clear cards that are easy to read on a phone at a job site or store aisle. You can switch between imperial and metric units, use common shapes such as rectangles, circles, and triangles, and adjust pricing assumptions to match your local supplier.
				</p>
				<p>
					For best results, measure each project section separately and add them together. Include a small waste factor for irregular edges, settling, compaction, and measurement errors. Then confirm the final order with your local material supplier, especially for mulch depth, bark type, or playground coverage where soil conditions and moisture can change the required volume. These calculators are built to give you a reliable planning estimate, reduce guesswork, and make it easier to order the right amount of material the first time.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<FAQ lang={lang} />
	</main>

	<Footer lang={lang} />
</Layout>
